From 5ab88d9a8960e75241965c1e48b3760544db264e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CrockMr <118761873+CrockMr@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 17:10:10 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Expose calculated health maxima in the oracle state dump

health[].maximum now carries Meitou's calculated HealthPart.MaxHp
instead of null, null when negative, non-finite or above 1e9, as the
native probe does. It is documented as calculated, not the original's
stored _maxHealth. In the 1 November setup heal receipts (unworn, full
health) the saved player matched part by part on both engines,
including a stump at 5 (Observed); spawned members of two races showed
the same value set on both engines, but not the same characters, and
the origin of their 125 per part is Unknown. Wear, prosthetics, robots
and later multiplier or scale changes remain Unknown.

The capture stays read-only; a test pins plain, scaled, worn, stump,
worn-away, NaN, infinite and above-cap parts and checks that the state
hash is unchanged. order stays null.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
